    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The request body is bound to `OwnerFieldsDto` (not the `Owner` entity), and the handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:145`).\n\n## Validations (in execution order)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must have the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **Framework Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto`** (`@Valid @RequestBody`, runs before the method body) \u2192 400 on any failure:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[0-9()+\\-.\\s]*$)`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `title` \u2014 enum `MR/MRS/MS/DR` (optional)\n   - `address` / `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)` (optional); `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)` (optional)\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n3. **`OwnerFieldsValidator.findMissingFields`** \u2014 blank check on `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and `address` (missing only if both `addressLine1` and flat `address` are blank) \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400). *(Runs after `resolveAddress`, side-effect #1 below.)*\n4. **`PostcodeValidator.isValidForCity`** \u2014 postcode must fall in the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region or null postcode passes) \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n5. **City capacity** \u2014 `countOwnersByCity(city) >= 50` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`) \u2192 `CityCapacityExceededException` (409).\n6. **`RegistrationDatePolicy.isAfterServerDate`** \u2014 registration date cannot be in the future \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n7. **Daily limit** \u2014 `countOwnersRegisteredOn(effectiveDate) >= 100` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`) \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (429). (`effectiveDate` = the date rolled forward past weekends/holidays.)\n8. **Telephone normalization** \u2014 validation happens inside the normalizer (E.164, +61 default, 8\u201315 digits) \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400). *(Also a side-effect \u2014 see below.)*\n9. **`DisposableEmailValidator.isDisposable`** \u2014 blocks `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` \u2192 `DisposableEmailException` (400).\n10. **Household duplicate** \u2014 unless the request declares `sharesHousehold=true`, `isHouseholdDuplicate` rejects a matching household \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n\n## Side-effects (in execution order)\n\n1. **`resolveAddress(ownerFieldsDto)`** \u2014 normalizes `addressLine1/2` and composes/normalizes the resolved `address` field on the DTO. *(Happens before validation #3.)*\n2. **DTO \u2192 `Owner` mapping** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`); `id` and `pets` are ignored/empty.\n3. **`owner.setTelephone(TelephoneNormalizer.normalize(...))`** \u2014 mutates telephone to E.164.\n4. **`owner.setEmail(EmailNormalizer.normalize(...))`** \u2014 lowercases/trims; null if blank.\n5. **`owner.setHouseholdId(HouseholdIdGenerator.generate(...))`** \u2014 SHA-256 hex prefix (12 chars) of normalized `lastName` + `postcode`; null when no postcode.\n6. **`owner.setDeclaredHouseholdMember(...)`** \u2014 from `sharesHousehold`.\n7. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 `@Transactional`; on a new owner it enriches before persisting:\n   - Mints `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, deduplicated by appending `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 via `existsByCustomerCode`.\n   - Sets `namesakeCount` (owners with same first+last name).\n   - Sets `householdSize` (owners sharing `householdId`, +1).\n   - Runs `possibleDuplicateDetector` (skipped if declared household member) and sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n   - **`@PrePersist` hook `resolveRegistrationDate`** re-resolves `registrationDate` to the effective business day at flush.\n   - `em.persist(owner)`.\n8. **`ownerAuditor.ownerCreated(owner)`** \u2014 writes an `AUDIT` INFO log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membership info).\n9. **`idempotencyKeyStore.remember(key, id)`** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header was supplied, stores key\u2192id in an in-memory map. *(There's also a matching pre-check at the top: if the key was seen before, it short-circuits and returns 200 with the existing owner, skipping everything above.)*\n10. **Response** \u2014 builds `OwnerDto` with `bulkSignupWarning` = (owners registered today > 80), sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, returns **201 Created**.\n\n## One caveat worth flagging\nThe `Owner` entity itself carries Bean Validation constraints (`@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city, and `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)` on telephone). These are **not** re-validated on this path \u2014 the entity is never `@Valid`-checked and is persisted directly \u2014 so the effective gate is the DTO constraints plus the imperative checks above."
